# Agent-memory writes with an unresolved Windows path create a literal
# "C:\..." directory at the repo root on Linux. It is not a real path and must
# never be committed; the agent tooling owns the underlying bug.
C:\\*

# Scratch probes. Agents and reviewers write throwaway kernel/derivation probes
# as zz*_test.go by convention while mutation-testing; they are measurement
# scaffolding, never a deliverable, and a stray `git add -A` should not be able
# to land one. No tracked file has ever used this prefix.
zz*_test.go

# =============================================================================
# Tracked-content negations
# =============================================================================
# The blanket `.*` rule above (and a few directory rules below it) matched 307
# files that are *already tracked* in this repository — including .github/
# workflows, .gitattributes, the entire .quality_assurance/ corpus, and eight
# .claude skills. A rule that ignores tracked content does not remove it; it
# silently drops new siblings from `git add`, so a new QA doc or a new workflow
# vanishes without an error. That is not hypothetical: it swallowed a set of
# research documents in this branch's history before being caught.
#
# These negations make the ignore file describe reality. They un-ignore only
# paths whose content is already committed; nothing new is exposed.

# Git and CI configuration.
!.gitattributes
!.github/
!.github/**

# Quality-assurance corpora. Every file under these is tracked repo content.
!.quality_assurance/
!.quality_assurance/**
!.e2e_quality_assurance/
!.e2e_quality_assurance/**
!.jules/
!.jules/**

# Claude skills whose definitions live in the repo.
!.claude/skills/corpus-comms-plumber/
!.claude/skills/corpus-comms-plumber/**
!.claude/skills/corpus-consumables-keeper/
!.claude/skills/corpus-consumables-keeper/**
!.claude/skills/corpus-critic/
!.claude/skills/corpus-critic/**
!.claude/skills/corpus-defense-auditor/
!.claude/skills/corpus-defense-auditor/**
!.claude/skills/corpus-doc-auditor/
!.claude/skills/corpus-doc-auditor/**
!.claude/skills/corpus-feature-tagging/
!.claude/skills/corpus-feature-tagging/**
!.claude/skills/corpus-jules-dispatcher/
!.claude/skills/corpus-jules-dispatcher/**
!.claude/skills/requirements-interrogator/
!.claude/skills/requirements-interrogator/**
!.agents/skills/spec-doc-sprint/
!.agents/skills/spec-doc-sprint/**

# Repository tooling. /scripts/ is ignored for local scratch, but these are
# checked-in quality gates.
!/scripts/deadcode-budget.sh
!/scripts/test_windows_path_identity.ps1
!/scripts/testdata/
!/scripts/testdata/**

# Subsystem specifications. Docs/Spec/ is listed as corpus-build scratch above,
# but its committed contents are deliverable documentation.
!Docs/Spec/
!Docs/Spec/**

# =============================================================================
# Safety floor — MUST REMAIN LAST
# =============================================================================
# Ignore rules are last-match-wins. The negations above re-expose whole
# directory trees, which would otherwise override the secret and noise guards
# declared earlier in this file: a config.json under .quality_assurance/ or
# .github/ became committable the moment those trees were un-ignored.
#
# Re-asserting them here restores the intended precedence. Nothing may be added
# below this block.

# Credentials and provider payloads. This is the one that matters.
**/config.json
**/config.*.json
config.json
**/*.secret
**/secrets.json
*.pem
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.key

# Local model prompt files.
**/CLAUDE.md
**/claude.md
**/GEMINI.md
**/gemini.md

# Runtime noise and build output.
*.log
*.exe
*.test
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite3-journal
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch probe tests (see the note above the original rule).
zz*_test.go

# Campaign runtime debris written by tests executing inside the package dir.
internal/campaign/.nerd/
internal/campaign/campaigns/
internal/campaign/log.txt
